# CODEOWNERS — who must approve changes to the MoonBite canonical repo.
#
# GitHub uses the LAST matching pattern for a given file. Anything not matched
# below falls through to the catch-all owner on the first line. Ownership only
# has teeth when branch protection has "Require review from Code Owners"
# enabled on the protected branch (see docs/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md).
#
# The goal: nobody can merge a change to consensus, proof-of-work, chain
# parameters, key handling, or CI/release plumbing without the maintainer's
# explicit review — even though anyone is free to fork and experiment.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Catch-all: the maintainer owns everything by default.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                               @moonbitecoin

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Consensus / proof-of-work / chain parameters — CRITICAL. A change here can
# hard-fork the chain or silently alter money supply. Owner review required.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/pow.py                         @moonbitecoin
/params.py                      @moonbitecoin
/merkle.py                      @moonbitecoin
/block.py                       @moonbitecoin
/transaction.py                 @moonbitecoin
/utxo.py                        @moonbitecoin
/store.py                       @moonbitecoin
/node.py                        @moonbitecoin
/full_node.py                   @moonbitecoin
/node_rpc_server.py             @moonbitecoin
/calc.py                        @moonbitecoin
/spv.py                         @moonbitecoin

